  <static seed="5" source="Library/PCC/BasicAlgebra/FunctionBasics/FunctionValuesByGraph20.pg">
    <statement><p>The graph of a function <m>f</m> is shown below.</p>
<!-- PTX:WARNING: PGML wanted to center align here. -->
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/evaluating-functions-3-image-1.png" width="40%"/>
<p>Use the given graph of <m>f</m>. If there is more than one answer to a question, you can use commas and the word <lq/>or<rq/>. When solving an equation for the variable <m>x</m>, your answer should be in the form <lq/>x=___<rq/>.</p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p>Evaluate <m>\displaystyle{f(0)}</m>.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{f(0)={}}</m><fillin characters="9" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Solve <m>\displaystyle{f(x)=2}</m>.</p>
<p><fillin characters="23" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>x = 2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>To evaluate <m>f(0)</m>, we understand that we have been given an <m>x</m>-value of <m>0</m>. On the graph, we draw a dotted vertical line at <m>x=0</m>, and it intersects the function<rsq/>s graph at <m>(0,-1)</m>. This implies <m>f(0)=-1</m>. See the graph below.</p>
<!-- PTX:WARNING: PGML wanted to center align here. -->
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/evaluating-functions-3-image-2.png" width="40%"/>
<p>To solve <m>f(x)=2</m>, we understand that we have been given a <m>y</m>-value of <m>2</m>. On the graph, we draw a dotted horizontal line at <m>y=2</m>, and it intersects the function<rsq/>s graph at <m>(2,2)</m>. This implies <m>f(2)=2</m>. See the graph below.</p>
<!-- PTX:WARNING: PGML wanted to center align here. -->
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/evaluating-functions-3-image-3.png" width="40%"/>
</solution>
